; A binding's colon announces its TYPE. `let a: 42` swallowed the parser's
; "expected BindingSpec" and bound 42 -- the optional annotation opened with
; any colon and its failure was dropped. It opens with the colon SIGN now
; (scaly.sgm, BindingAnnotation), so the error stands. 2026-10-04.
; xfail: expected BindingSpec

let a: 42
if a = 42
    print "PASS"
